// Copyright (c) 2026 Roshan. All rights reserved.// Proprietary license — see LICENSE file for details.package com.roshan.persona.security.integrity/** * NOUS — Integrity check state (Module 12, Pillar 1: Permission & Integrity). * * Result of a zero-trust integrity verification performed by * [ZeroTrustIntegrityManager] using Google Play Integrity API. * * Strategy §12.1: *   - **VERIFIED** — app is genuine, device is trusted, account is legitimate. *     All sensitive operations allowed. *   - **PARTIAL** — some checks failed but operation allowed with warning. *     Sensitive operations allowed but logged; user shown a soft warning. *   - **FAILED** — operation blocked. NOUS refuses to perform sensitive *     operations (credential vault access, backup/restore, banking app guard). * * The state is computed from three sub-checks (app, device, account) and the * overall state is the worst-case (FAILED > PARTIAL > VERIFIED). * * @see ZeroTrustIntegrityManager */sealed interface IntegrityCheckState {    /**     * The signing certificate, app version, and package name all match what     * Google Play expects; device passes Play Integrity; user account is real.     *     * @param requestHash opaque hash bound to a specific request (optional,     *   used to prevent replay of integrity tokens).     * @param verifiedAt epoch millis when verification succeeded.     */    data class Verified(        val requestHash: String? = null,        val verifiedAt: Long = System.currentTimeMillis(),    ) : IntegrityCheckState    /**     * One or more checks failed but the operation can proceed with a warning.     *     * Example: device passes Play Integrity but the app is being sideloaded     * (account check is unavailable); credential vault access is allowed but     * logged with elevated audit level.     *     * @param failedChecks human-readable list of which sub-checks failed     *   (e.g., "account_verification_unavailable", "play_protection_warning").     * @param verifiedAt epoch millis when verification was attempted.     */    data class Partial(        val failedChecks: List<String>,        val verifiedAt: Long = System.currentTimeMillis(),    ) : IntegrityCheckState    /**     * Integrity check definitively failed — operation MUST be blocked.     *     * Triggered when: app is repackaged/modified, device is rooted with     * Play Protection disabled, or integrity token request itself failed.     *     * @param reason machine-readable reason code (e.g., "app_modified",     *   "device_rooted", "token_request_failed").     * @param detail human-readable detail for logging (never shown to user).     * @param verifiedAt epoch millis when verification failed.     */    data class Failed(        val reason: String,        val detail: String? = null,        val verifiedAt: Long = System.currentTimeMillis(),    ) : IntegrityCheckState}